          "name": "calculate_leave",
          "source": "mcp:handbook",
          "ms": 603,
          "output": "{\n  \"start\": \"2026-12-19 (Sat)\",\n  \"end\": \"2027-01-10 (Sun)\",\n  \"region\": \"DE-BE\",\n  \"by_year\": {\n    \"2026\": {\n      \"leave_days\": 8,\n      \"leave_dates\": [\n        \"2026-12-21 (Mon)\",\n        \"2026-12-22 (Tue)\",\n        \"2026-12-23 (Wed)\",\n        \"2026-12-24 (Thu)\",\n        \"2026-12-28 (Mon)\",\n        \"2026-12-29 (Tue)\",\n        \"2026-12-30 (Wed)\",\n        \"2026-12-31 (Thu)\"\n      ],\n      \"public_holidays\": [\n        \"2026-12-25 (Fri) Erster Weihnachtstag\",\n        \"2026-12-26 (Sat) Zweiter Weihnachtstag\"\n      ],\n      \"weekend_days\": 3\n    },\n    \"2027\": {\n      \"leave_days\": 5,\n      \"leave_dates\": [\n        \"2027-01-04 (Mon)\",\n        \"2027-01-05 (Tue)\",\n        \"2027-01-06 (Wed)\",\n        \"2027-01-07 (Thu)\",\n        \"2027-01-08 (Fri)\"\n      ],\n      \"public_holidays\": [\n        \"2027-01-01 (Fri) Neujahr\"\n      ],\n      \"weekend_days\": 4\n    }\n  },\n  \"total_leave_days\": 13\n}",
          "is_error": false
        },
        {
          "type": "llm_start",
          "id": "01a12ff4-436a-76a1-8143-19031f116b66",
          "turn": 2,
          "node": "model",
          "message_count": 4
        },
        {
          "type": "llm_end",
          "id": "01a12ff4-436a-76a1-8143-19031f116b66",
          "turn": 2,
          "ms": 3690,
          "thinking": "2026 falls short by 3 days against the requirement of 8, while only 5 remain available, whereas 2027 easily fits using just 5 of its 28 days. I could offer to check for an alternative arrangement that stays within the 5-day limit in 2026, but I'll keep this brief and just offer to verify if asked.",
          "text": "It doesn't work with your balances as they stand.\n\n- **2026:** you'd need 8 leave days (21–24 and 28–31 Dec), but you only have 5. That's 3 days short.\n- **2027:** you'd need 5 leave days (4–8 Jan), and you have 28, so that's fine. Neujahr (1 Jan) is a public holiday and uses no leave.\n\nThe total is 13 leave days. Christmas Day (Fri 25 Dec) is a public holiday and 26 Dec falls on a Saturday, so neither uses leave.\n\nI can check alternative dates that fit within your 5 remaining 2026 days if you'd like.",
          "tool_calls": [],
          "stop_reason": "stop",
          "tokens": {
